    "Appeal to the original instincts of Colleagues 1, 8, 11, 12, 18, and 20 from Round 0. Remind them why they instinctively selected F before Camp C's hyper-literal, mechanical concordance crusade derailed the deliberation.",
    "Present a gracious, conciliatory tone: praise Camp C's philological acumen on line 734, but warn against falling into the trap of 'concordance literalism' at the expense of literary-critical item design. In university literature exams, the question is testing mastery of Chaucer's rhyme techniques (including *rime riche* and phonology), where F signifies that all listed items are reconciled by Chaucerian prosodic rules."
  ]
},
